        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@arkriny (and @justinmk, and @bfredl, in case this requires high code base knowledge level of input), this seems to only partially solve the linked issue. The title is combined with window's attributes only if the title is a string (which implies the `FloatTitle` / `FloatFooter` highlight groups), but not when the title is text-hl chunks. Here is the repro:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'FloatTitle', { fg = 'Green' })\r\n\r\n_G.show_floatwin = function()\r\n  vim.api.nvim_open_win(0, false, {\r\n    relative = 'editor',\r\n    width = 20,\r\n    height = 3,\r\n    row = 1,\r\n    col = 1,\r\n    border = 'single',\r\n    -- String title works\r\n    title = '     mytitle     ',\r\n    -- Chunks title does not work\r\n    -- title = { { '     mytitle     ', 'FloatTitle' } },\r\n  })\r\nend\r\n``` \r\n\r\nHere how the fist (string title) and second (chunks title) look:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2880\" height=\"1734\" alt=\"screenshot_2026-07-20_15:45:19\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/427bdcfe-ebb9-4468-aa4e-003c5df738e3\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2880\" height=\"1734\" alt=\"screenshot_2026-07-20_15:45:58\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/038e12a3-b4bb-4e21-b32b-19ec3af9fbca\" />\r\n\r\n",
            "created_at": "2026-07-20T12:47:50Z",
